696-174b-5aa6-a361-d4fb1513898f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(\\sqrt{q+1}+2)}{q-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496916} {:answer/id #uuid "beea4dc9-8883-552c-ac78-4a1888f63aac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(\\sqrt{q+1}+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497047} {:answer/id #uuid "c5c5c02f-1750-5fe2-84d3-9f069116c389" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4(\\sqrt{q+1}+2)}{q-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497063}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5c5c02f-1750-5fe2-84d3-9f069116c389" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4(\\sqrt{q+1}+2)}{q-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497063} :answer-field/id #uuid "352e22d3-3322-5945-aacd-bbb5be700ed3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497240}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1c076968-69eb-5008-a15f-3101901a7753" :question/math-academy-id "q-111085" :question/problem "Rationalize the denominator of $\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{q+1}-2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{q+1}+2.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{q+1}+2,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{q+1}-2} &= \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{q+1}-2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{q+1}+2}{\\sqrt{q+1}+2} \\\\ &= \\frac{4(\\sqrt{q+1}+2)}{(\\sqrt{q+1}-2)(\\sqrt{q+1}+2)} \\\\ &= \\frac{4(\\sqrt{q+1}+2)}{(\\sqrt{q+1})^{2}-{2}^{2}} \\\\ &= \\frac{4(\\sqrt{q+1}+2)}{q+1-4} \\\\ &= \\frac{4(\\sqrt{q+1}+2)}{q-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497354 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b65670a-a896-5610-82ac-5751ceff85c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12(\\sqrt{x+3}+\\sqrt{x+5})}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496715} {:answer/id #uuid "4ef52864-87e6-5b65-8775-27fca6c3a068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6(\\sqrt{x+3}+\\sqrt{x+5})}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496832} {:answer/id #uuid "82b190a0-3b5e-5790-9137-dada26dc5d6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12(\\sqrt{x+3}+\\sqrt{x+5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496925} {:answer/id #uuid "cff26320-aaef-57fe-a31f-7c3b21af878a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6(\\sqrt{x+3}+\\sqrt{x+5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497087} {:answer/id #uuid "d2128cd1-c593-59ee-8c09-21ce7bd84ce2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6(\\sqrt{x+3}+\\sqrt{x+5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2128cd1-c593-59ee-8c09-21ce7bd84ce2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6(\\sqrt{x+3}+\\sqrt{x+5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497096} :answer-field/id #uuid "e48e28cb-69c5-5ec3-b0b0-45cd22625ed2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497310}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "48232a69-9972-5f32-be1d-adbffa500e27" :question/math-academy-id "q-296049" :question/problem "Rationalize the denominator of $\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{x+3}-\\sqrt{x+5}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{x+3}+\\sqrt{x+5}.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{x+3}+\\sqrt{x+5},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{x+3}-\\sqrt{x+5}} &= \\frac{12}{\\sqrt{x+3}-\\sqrt{x+5}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{x+3}+\\sqrt{x+5}}{\\sqrt{x+3}+\\sqrt{x+5}} \\\\ &= \\frac{12(\\sqrt{x+3}+\\sqrt{x+5})}{(\\sqrt{x+3}+\\sqrt{x+5})(\\sqrt{x+3}+\\sqrt{x+5})} \\\\ &= \\frac{12(\\sqrt{x+3}+\\sqrt{x+5})}{(\\sqrt{x+3})^{2}-(\\sqrt{x+5})^{2}} \\\\ &= \\frac{12(\\sqrt{x+3}+\\sqrt{x+5})}{(x+3)-(x+5)} \\\\ &= \\frac{12(\\sqrt{x+3}+\\sqrt{x+5})}{-2} \\\\ &= -6(\\sqrt{x+3}+\\sqrt{x+5})\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497360 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bb361c6-6dd5-552c-a427-a36cf070b655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{w(\\sqrt{2w+3}+1)}{w+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496679} {:answer/id #uuid "4881d5c1-1bbc-586e-9272-b79e718a7ae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{w(\\sqrt{2w+3}+1)}{w+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496822} {:answer/id #uuid "58b04e7f-48fb-5d60-9894-e699ad85fce0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2w+3}+2}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496845} {:answer/id #uuid "59ba9695-6e1c-5180-8ee9-758ebad42ea3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2w+3}+4}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496851} {:answer/id #uuid "9fc00c71-a5e7-57f3-b1b5-fd9dc5eab57b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2w+3}+1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9fc00c71-a5e7-57f3-b1b5-fd9dc5eab57b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2w+3}+1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496991} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bc4d4eb-b093-5f42-bf15-0372a2d6d50b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497258}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "58d0d2af-1f8e-5b5b-ada1-d6636471e4c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-111092" :question/problem "Rationalize the denominator of $\\frac{w+1}{\\sqrt{2w+3}-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{2w+3}+1.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{2w+3}+1,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{w+1}{\\sqrt{2w+3}-1} &= \\frac{w+1}{\\sqrt{2w+3}-1}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2w+3}+1}{\\sqrt{2w+3}+1} \\\\ &= \\frac{(w+1)(\\sqrt{2w+3}+1)}{(\\sqrt{2w+3}-1)(\\sqrt{2w+3}+1)} \\\\ &= \\frac{(w+1)(\\sqrt{2w+3}+1)}{(\\sqrt{2w+3})^{2}-{1}^{2}} \\\\ &= \\frac{(w+1)(\\sqrt{2w+3}+1)}{2w+3-1} \\\\ &= \\frac{(w+1)(\\sqrt{2w+3}+1)}{2w+2} \\\\ &= \\frac{\\cancel{(w+1)}(\\sqrt{2w+3}+1)}{2\\cancel{(w+1)}} \\\\ &= \\frac{\\sqrt{2w+3}+1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497392 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59c0abeb-efea-5346-a12d-6aceb41e5d82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2c+5)(2c-5)(\\sqrt{2c-1}-2)}{c}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496852} {:answer/id #uuid "5b6d0a3a-7076-5fdb-9621-e69c7e602ff2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2c+5)(2c-5)(\\sqrt{2c-1}-2)}{c-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496858} {:answer/id #uuid "6b4043b8-d542-56a8-94c3-4a171b378921" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2c-5)(\\sqrt{2c-1}-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496889} {:answer/id #uuid "d09d9917-b956-5f74-8457-7b67b79b18b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2c+5)(2c-5)(\\sqrt{2c-1}-2)}{c+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497090} {:answer/id #uuid "e3220828-f713-5b43-83e7-461b5c071967" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2c+5)(\\sqrt{2c-1}-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3220828-f713-5b43-83e7-461b5c071967" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2c+5)(\\sqrt{2c-1}-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497145} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b21d62e-53c1-50ce-9ab2-68ee95cacfa9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b52a407e-c533-5755-83ae-d5bfaf9c5559" :question/math-academy-id "q-111090" :question/problem "Rationalize the denominator of $\\frac{4{c}^{2}-25}{\\sqrt{2c-1}+2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{2c-1}-2.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{2c-1}-2,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4{c}^{2}-25}{\\sqrt{2c-1}+2} &= \\frac{4{c}^{2}-25}{\\sqrt{2c-1}+2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2c-1}-2}{\\sqrt{2c-1}-2} \\\\ &= \\frac{(4{c}^{2}-25)(\\sqrt{2c-1}-2)}{(\\sqrt{2c-1}+2)(\\sqrt{2c-1}-2)} \\\\ &= \\frac{(4{c}^{2}-25)(\\sqrt{2c-1}-2)}{(\\sqrt{2c-1})^{2}-{2}^{2}} \\\\ &= \\frac{(2c+5)(2c-5)(\\sqrt{2c-1}-2)}{2c-1-4} \\\\ &= \\frac{(2c+5)(2c-5)(\\sqrt{2c-1}-2)}{2c-5} \\\\ &= \\frac{(2c+5)\\cancel{(2c-5)}(\\sqrt{2c-1}-2)}{\\cancel{2c-5}} \\\\ &= (2c+5)(\\sqrt{2c-1}-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497414 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ed6f177-f0a7-51b5-91f1-45cc3525ec42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2w}+\\sqrt{6}}{w-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496724} {:answer/id #uuid "297af7c5-9d20-5ec8-b43e-b61d43129d8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(\\sqrt{2w}-\\sqrt{6})}{w-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496749} {:answer/id #uuid "2f7e0d94-a5f9-5adf-866f-e3b8e6f6df78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2w}-\\sqrt{6}}{w-6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496762} {:answer/id #uuid "89c3d947-dd0c-55f3-b1d7-b34cdac78a47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2w}+\\sqrt{6}}{w-6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496946} {:answer/id #uuid "d6e1d989-f66b-52e3-97f0-bbb5658af8d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(\\sqrt{2w}+\\sqrt{6})}{w-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497110}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ed6f177-f0a7-51b5-91f1-45cc3525ec42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2w}+\\sqrt{6}}{w-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496724} :answer-field/id #uuid "9306fa45-f979-577d-88b6-95185ddf9d49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497285}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f7189aac-304f-5339-9ec2-dd1037933cdd" :question/math-academy-id "q-85407" :question/problem "Rationalize the denominator of $\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2w}-\\sqrt{6}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{2w}+\\sqrt{6}.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{2w}+\\sqrt{6},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2w}-\\sqrt{6}} &= \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2w}-\\sqrt{6}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2w}+\\sqrt{6}}{\\sqrt{2w}+\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ &= \\frac{2(\\sqrt{2w}+\\sqrt{6})}{(\\sqrt{2w}-\\sqrt{6})(\\sqrt{2w}+\\sqrt{6})} \\\\ &= \\frac{2(\\sqrt{2w}+\\sqrt{6})}{(\\sqrt{2w})^{2}-(\\sqrt{6})^{2}} \\\\ &= \\frac{2(\\sqrt{2w}+\\sqrt{6})}{2w-6} \\\\ &= \\frac{2(\\sqrt{2w}+\\sqrt{6})}{2(w-3)} \\\\ &= \\frac{\\sqrt{2w}+\\sqrt{6}}{w-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498496 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44c2ade4-f5ae-5da7-92f6-13439bcfb0e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497952} {:answer/id #uuid "95da5035-aa03-5fd9-9934-1276912a83bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498140} {:answer/id #uuid "b8b6c976-6a54-5ca3-9ff2-d2becacd1202" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498210} {:answer/id #uuid "c096d1ec-d8c4-558c-995c-07ceb55cc2fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498227} {:answer/id #uuid "f20d18bf-7e28-55a2-8282-878eb89dcddf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44c2ade4-f5ae-5da7-92f6-13439bcfb0e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497952} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1a3138f-68f7-5a88-b85b-47ce925e2372" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498446}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "13de8b24-aaa0-5ec2-ad2b-e4d7d0eec094" :question/math-academy-id "q-135712" :question/problem "Given that $q\\ge 0,$ simplify $12q-|-2q|.$" :question/worked-solution "Firstly, since $|-a|=|a|,$ we can write our expression as\n\n$$\n12q-|2q|.\n$$\n\nThen, we distribute the absolute value over the multiplication. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12q-|2q| &= 12q-|2|\\cdot |q| \\\\ &= 12q-2\\cdot |q| \\\\ &= 12q-2|q|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $q\\ge 0,$ we have that $|q|=q.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12q-2|q| &= 12q-2q \\\\ &= 10q.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498498 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6da3c059-e7a2-561d-b24f-ae1a025126bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|s|+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498066} {:answer/id #uuid "aa13e59a-2a4d-535a-9aff-88818af6a236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4|s|+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498176} {:answer/id #uuid "ae900989-fa31-5ec7-a8af-afd82d4149e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4s-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498187} {:answer/id #uuid "ccc825dd-39a6-5b11-a839-62ca6e000973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4|s|+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498260} {:answer/id #uuid "db6d064b-135a-5826-aa11-e1ee2c639e09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4s+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa13e59a-2a4d-535a-9aff-88818af6a236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4|s|+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498176} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5c1e571-065f-56e1-b547-c5d8576a10bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498481}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "176b69af-2301-5857-a64b-7b0669d9dca3" :question/math-academy-id "q-52130" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $2\\cdot |-2s|+3.$" :question/worked-solution "Firstly, since $|-a|=|a|,$ we can write our expression as\n\n$$\n2\\cdot |2s|+3.\n$$\n\nThen, we distribute the absolute value over the multiplication, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot |2s|+3 &= 2\\cdot |2|\\cdot |s|+3 \\\\ &= 2\\cdot 2\\cdot |s|+3 \\\\ &= 4|s|+3\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498503 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60880834-349f-5d68-8a44-911ad22f6c01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60880834-349f-5d68-8a44-911ad22f6c01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498028} :answer-field/id #uuid "d65d922c-2c94-5032-93b1-bec03c4b0c50" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498466}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1fe649a3-8b82-51f4-b2a6-c51dc888b658" :question/math-academy-id "q-133741" :question/problem "![](images/e6/e60f532665c5fdae2a9fdcebdc84af674cd9bdb8b1c820c7b766d565af74f1d1.png)\n\nA utility pole is located on the edge of Diana's land, as shown above. The distance from the right edge of Diana's plot to the pole is $x-3$ meters. Find the distance to the pole from the left edge as a function of $x.$\n\nThe required distance is \n{{field-1}}\nmeters." :question/worked-solution "In part 1, we found that the length of Diana's plot is $2x$ meters.\n\nTo find the required distance, we need to subtract polynomials $2x$ and $x-3:$\n\nWe put a minus sign between the two polynomials, distribute it over the second polynomial, collect like terms, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2x)-(x-3) &= 2x-x+3 \\\\ &= (2-1)x+3 \\\\ &= x+3\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498516 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b3a0149-a358-598f-ab2f-8bf802871f13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b3a0149-a358-598f-ab2f-8bf802871f13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497888} :answer-field/id #uuid "de5378f0-df33-5b0f-a0f2-946b1547ce91" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "33fd3371-4ae9-5c23-8649-ebbfb1a6d062" :question/math-academy-id "q-133742" :question/problem "![](images/8a/8a0c1f1814427b696cff8ef4aaa7357744855a75598d5ed878dd93b022ed59de.png)\n\nDiana's neighbor to the south, Ron, has a land plot of area ${x}^{2}+x-6$ square meters, as shown in the picture. Given that the length of Ron's plot of land is $x+3$ meters, what is the width of the plot in terms of $x?$\n\nRon's plot width is\n{{field-1}}\nmeters." :question/worked-solution "To find the required width, we need to factor the expression ${x}^{2}+x-6.$ \n\nFirst, we find the factor pairs of the constant term $(-6).$ The constant term is negative, so that means one of the factors is negative, and the other is positive:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & \\times (-6) \\\\ (-1) & \\times 6 \\\\ 2 & \\times (-3) \\\\ (-2) & \\times 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find which factor pair adds up to the coefficient of the linear term $3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+(-6) & =-5 & \\times  \\\\ -1+6 & =5 & \\times  \\\\ 2+(-3) & =-1 & \\times  \\\\ -2+3 & =1 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the factor pair identified above, write the linear term as $x=-2x+3x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+x-6 & ={x}^{2}-2x+3x-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the first two terms and the last two terms separately, and then factor the expression completely:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x+3x-6 &= ({x}^{2}-2x)+(3x-6) \\\\ &= x(x-2)+3(x-2) \\\\ &= (x-2)(x+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we conclude that the width must be $x-2$ meters.  \n\n![](images/e6/e6330144c5ee2a25038e4378f442957a48df0e8dc06fa460f88863c4645fbecd.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498552 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fc0bc59-3785-5eda-b8fc-f947d9ab58ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-2(k)^{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497835} {:answer/id #uuid "22d42365-3034-57f9-b80d-03413fa89807" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{k}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497872} {:answer/id #uuid "4cfef805-d8bd-5a29-b7b3-ef894a92d11c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2{k}^{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497976} {:answer/id #uuid "8824de24-d3dc-5d98-b0ca-f43ee7699f9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{k}^{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498113} {:answer/id #uuid "bf56fbd2-f5c2-579c-8ebb-6d499c95b621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{k}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8824de24-d3dc-5d98-b0ca-f43ee7699f9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{k}^{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498113} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbfbd916-b1d3-545a-8514-bc1cb5dfc2a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498459}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7d1d6d3a-1caf-53a1-9cd7-47e7cd04105c" :question/math-academy-id "q-78941" :question/problem "$|-\\frac{2{k}^{2}}{3}|=$" :question/worked-solution "Firstly, since $|-a|=|a|,$ we can write our expression as\n\n$$\n|\\frac{2{k}^{2}}{3}|.\n$$\n\nThen, we distribute the absolute value over the multiplication and division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\frac{2{k}^{2}}{3}| &= \\frac{|2{k}^{2}|}{|3|} \\\\ &= \\frac{|2|\\cdot |{k}^{2}|}{3} \\\\ &= \\frac{2|{k}^{2}|}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${k}^{2}\\ge 0$ for any real $k,$ we have that $|{k}^{2}|={k}^{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2|{k}^{2}|}{3} & =\\frac{2{k}^{2}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498565 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46756f20-d863-59c7-8831-681121f75c44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "150" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46756f20-d863-59c7-8831-681121f75c44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "150" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497961} :answer-field/id #uuid "594314f7-b3c5-5c92-a963-511c915f65b3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498397}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9c4d0824-bd55-5a10-a7aa-4a3af941bdbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-133744" :question/problem "If $x=12\\,\\text{m},$ what is the area of Ron's land plot?\n\nArea $\\,=$\n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m}}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we have to evaluate the polynomial ${x}^{2}+x-6$ at $x=12.$\n\nSo, we substitute $x=12$ into the polynomial and simplify: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+x-6 &= (12)^{2}+(12)-6 \\\\ &= 144+12-6 \\\\ &= 150\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area is $150\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498566 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d8d48f2-1909-5037-a943-3e29c5504ed2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d8d48f2-1909-5037-a943-3e29c5504ed2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497830} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd265226-df27-5582-ae30-81c64076603e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498471}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9c4f0f4c-398e-580b-8ef0-276b7b031bf0" :question/math-academy-id "q-133739" :question/problem "Expressed as a polynomial in terms of $x,$ the length of Diana's plot of land is{{field-1}}\nmeters." :question/worked-solution "The width of the plot is $x-1$ meters, and its area is $2{x}^{2}-2x$ square meters. Since the $\\text{area}=\\text{length}\\times \\text{width},$ we factor the expression for the area to find the length.\n\nFirst, we find the $\\text{GCF}$ of the two terms:\n\n$$\n\\text{GCF}(2{x}^{2},-2x)=2x\n$$\n\nThen, we rewrite each term in the original expression as a product with the $\\text{GCF}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-2x &= (2x\\cdot x)+(2x\\cdot (-1))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we write the $\\text{GCF}$ outside the parentheses and keep the remaining terms inside:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2x\\cdot x)+(2x\\cdot (-1)) &= 2x(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we conclude that the length of the plot must be $2x$ meters.\n\n![](images/da/dadb8090017f300275d803d488d401435b4f0e29b26ddf19e5542dba60a6bec4.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498592 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21bf1704-ae50-5b54-a182-325089ab00d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23{x}^{2}" :db/id #ed